The placement's stops with the log's Stagger breaks' holds (2026-11-27, the break's open points; dropped)

The placement (logcasts.ts passStops, pass 2) reads the placed casts' stops and the unplaced cast events'; with engine
assumption break-hold the engine also holds every clock 14 frames at each logged break, which the placement didn't
know: a cast pressed before a break whose first landing comes after it is placed from that landing as if nothing held
it (fc63a2001251: Typhoeus's 99.03 s combo, the replay's INSIDE at 102.33 s). This adds the breaks' holds (as holds.ts
breakStops, inlined: holds.ts imports logcasts.ts) to pass 2's stops. Measured (measure --patch against e2e6f3f's
snapshots): development unchanged (fc63 "other": totals only), earlier pending 1 worse (d774 damage −0.4 → −0.5%),
1 mixed (3aa6 plain 419 → 418, damage 1.0 → −0.1%), hold-outs unchanged. Dropped: a held start (heldStart) needs the
log's cast event near it, which few casts across a break have, so nearly nothing moves. Would matter once the casts'
starts read the breaks' holds without an event (a rule for that is the next step if fc63's INSIDE is to go).

